*  s184 seat7 CONTROL for leafwide_span_dyncs_alt: IDENTICAL shape, one ingredient removed.
*  The charset is written inline so it constant-folds to a static IP-relative table
*  (lea rdi,[rip+.C1]) and the SPAN box makes ZERO flat [rsp+N] operand reads.  Arming still
*  re-homes the leaf cell to rbp and still widens the carve by 16 -- and this program is
*  GREEN in BOTH arms.  That is the whole argument: the defect is not the re-home and not
*  the ALT arm, it is the un-rebased flat SPINE OPERAND read inside the re-homed box.
          epsilon        =
          digits         = '0123456789'
          T              = 'Name'
          T              POS(0) ANY(&UCASE &LCASE)
+                        (SPAN( digits &UCASE '_' &LCASE) | epsilon) RPOS(0)       :S(OK)F(NO)
OK        OUTPUT         = 'bare'                                                  :(END)
NO        OUTPUT         = 'quoted'
END
